# Build-tool writes a live `tamga index` run leaves behind across the 9
# family units in this fixture. Mirrors the walker's own built-in ignore
# overlay (src/detect/walker.rs) plus a few tool-specific extras -- none of
# this should ever be committed; a clean `git status` after a live run
# proves tamga only made the writes it discloses in repo_writes.
node_modules/
dist/
build/
out/
target/
bin/
obj/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.gradle/
.idea/
.vs/
Pods/
bower_components/
.next/
.turbo/
coverage/
cmake-build-*/
vendor/
.bundle/
Gemfile.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml
package-lock.json
composer.lock
index.scip
*.scip
*.log

# frontend/tsconfig.json: a real `scip-typescript index --cwd frontend`
# (live-verified, M8) writes a bare `{}` tsconfig.json at the scanned root
# when none exists there -- true even with `ts_mode: Ts` (no
# `--infer-tsconfig` flag involved), a scip-typescript behavior tamga
# doesn't control or currently disclose via `repo_writes`. Ignored here so
# a live run doesn't dirty the committed fixture; see task-9-report.md's
# concerns section for the full writeup.
frontend/tsconfig.json
